---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: 'About',
    url: new URL('/about/', SITE.url).href,
    description: 'AI Founder Files profiles one AI founder and their company in depth every week: one founder, one company, one deep dive.',
    inLanguage: 'en-GB',
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
    about: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization`, name: SITE.name, url: SITE.url, logo: `${SITE.url}/icon-512.png` },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL('/', SITE.url).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: new URL('/about/', SITE.url).href },
    ],
  },
];
---
<PageLayout
  title="About"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  description="AI Founder Files profiles one AI founder and their company in depth every week: one founder, one company, one deep dive."
  label="About"
  heading="One founder. One company. One deep dive."
>
  <p>
    AI Founder Files is a weekly publication. Every week we open one file: the founder, the product, the funding and the business model behind a new AI company, told in full.
  </p>

  <h2>What a file covers</h2>
  <p>Every Founder File follows the same shape, so you can read it quickly or go deep:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The File.</strong> A fact box at the top: founder, company, when it was founded, where it’s based, its sector, stage and funding. Where something isn’t public, it says “Undisclosed” rather than guessing.</li>
    <li><strong>The story.</strong> Who the founder is, the problem they set out to solve, what the product does and how the company makes money.</li>
    <li><strong>The sources.</strong> Every file ends with the documents, filings, interviews and announcements it draws on.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why one at a time</h2>
  <p>
    Most coverage of AI companies is a headline about a funding round. We think a single company deserves a full read: what is it, who is behind it, who is paying for it, and whether the business holds together. One a week keeps us honest about depth.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> sets out the rules: coverage is never paid for, sponsored content is always labelled, and how we fact-check and correct our work.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    To get the weekly file, <a href="/subscribe/">subscribe</a>. To flag a mistake, see <a href="/editorial-policy/#corrections">how to request a correction</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
